## In this guide

- [Council tax](/support/money-off-bills/council-tax/): the Disabled Band Reduction Scheme, severe mental impairment discounts and carer discounts
- [Energy and water](/support/money-off-bills/energy-and-water/): the Warm Home Discount, Priority Services Register, WaterSure and cold weather help
- [Phone, broadband and TV](/support/money-off-bills/phone-broadband-and-tv/): social tariffs, free directory enquiries and TV licence discounts

## Check your benefits first

Many discounts depend on getting a **means-tested benefit**, such as Universal Credit or Pension Credit. Getting **PIP, DLA or Attendance Allowance** can increase some means-tested benefits, or help you qualify for them, which then unlocks these discounts. Use a free **benefits calculator**, such as Turn2us or entitledto, to check.
